	"changelog": "\n2026.09.10: Fixed playlists (saved playlists, and playlists opened from search results or a followed channel) announcing \"Playback ended\" instead of playing with Enter/F7, and fixed replaying the last item afterward. Saved settings, playlists, and subscriptions now survive add-on updates and reinstalls instead of being erased. Added Shorts as a search type on the Search and Download tab, and fixed it returning no results right after shipping. Fixed the search type list losing Live (and Shorts) after switching interface language. Updated the Control+F1 shortcut help text on the Search and Download and Playlists tabs to match current shortcuts.\n2026.09.02: Confirmed compatibility with NVDA 2026.2 (released 2026-08-31) and updated lastTestedNVDAVersion accordingly. Reviewed NVDA 2026.2's developer changelog (new Magnifier, touch gestures, speech dictionaries, braille auto-scroll, deprecated speechDictHandler constants) and confirmed none of it affects this add-on's code, since this add-on does not use any of those APIs - no functional code changes were needed.\n2026.08.25: Fixed MP4 downloads failing outright while MP3 downloads kept working normally. The MP4 download format selector only matched a video that YouTube had already muxed together with its audio into one file - YouTube increasingly does not offer such a combined format at all for many videos anymore, so the download matched nothing and failed. MP4 downloads now request the best available video and audio streams separately and mux them together with the bundled ffmpeg (same as this add-on already does for live playback and MP3 extraction), which works regardless of whether YouTube offers a combined format for a given video.\n2026.08.20: Fixed the automatic yt-dlp update checker only checking once every 24 hours, which made it easy to reasonably believe automatic updates were not working at all - it now checks on every NVDA startup instead (still only if enabled in Settings). Added a self-check that runs after a real restart to verify a yt-dlp update that reported success actually took effect, and warns you plainly if it did not (most likely causes: antivirus/Windows Defender blocking the newly-written files, or another NVDA installation on this computer) instead of silently staying on the old version with no explanation. Updated the bundled yt-dlp library to the latest stable release (2026.08.19).\n2026.08.18: Updated the bundled yt-dlp library (2026.07.04 to a 2026.08.17 pre-release build) to fix YouTube extraction breaking for pasted links (\"Could not fetch data\") - YouTube had changed something extraction-dependent since the previous release, and yt-dlp's maintainers had already shipped several fix builds ahead of their next stable release. Currently-live broadcasts now open directly in the user's default browser instead of playing inside the add-on, since the browser's own native YouTube player handles live playback more reliably than the bundled offline media player ever could. Added a \"Live\" search type alongside Video/Playlist/Channel, to find currently-live broadcasts by keyword directly from the Search and Download tab (previously only reachable per-channel via the Subscriptions tab's Live section). Also fixes an unrelated ordinary-video playback bug where mpv's own internal link resolver was incorrectly re-engaging on links this add-on had already resolved itself, occasionally cutting playback short before the end.\n2026.07.19: Full-featured release. Search, play, and download YouTube videos, playlists, and channels entirely by keyboard - audio playback with full transport control (play/pause, seek, volume, speed, previous/next with automatic continue), a sleep timer, personal playlist management, and a Subscriptions tab that browses a followed channel's Videos, Shorts, Live, and Playlists the way YouTube itself organizes them. Download to MP3 or MP4 with selectable quality, auto-sorted into folders by playlist or channel name. Full English/Thai interface with instant switching (Control+T).\n",
